window.products.push({"id":1191060,"name":"SF Cable 35ft Cat 6A Unshielded (UTP) Ethernet Network Cable, 500MHz, 24AWG - Black","category":"electronics","retail price":15.25,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51fM2apbHhL._SL1000_.jpg","description":"SF Cable patch cables are made of 100% bare copper wire and 50 micron gold plated RJ45 plugs. Why 50 micron? We do not use CCA (aluminum wire). What is CCA? 10G Cat.6A cabling provides transmission performance that excceeds the industry standard Cat.6 parameters and supports the operation of 10GBASE-T over 100 meter. 10G Cat.6A solutions are qualified for frequencies up to 500MHz. Performance conforms to proposed Cat.6A channel requirement of TIA/EIA-568-B-2-10 class EA ISO/IEC 11801, CENELEC EN 50173 and IEEE802.3an Performance conforms to proposed Cat.6A channel requirement of TIA/EIA-568-B-2-10 class EA ISO/IEC 11801, CENELEC EN 50173 and IEEE802.3an Designed For: Network Adapters, Hubs, Switches, Routers, DSL/Cable Modems, Patch Panels and other Computer Networking applications. Designed For: Network Adapters, Hubs, Switches, Routers, DSL/Cable Modems, Patch Panels and other Computer Networking applications. 35ft Cat.6A Patch Cable Molded 35ft Cat.6A Patch Cable Molded Color Available: Black, Blue, Gray, Green, Red, White, and Yellow Color Available: Black, Blue, Gray, Green, Red, White, and Yellow Application 10GBASE-T Ethernet 10GBASE-T Ethernet 1000BASE-TX Fast Ethernet 1000BASE-TX Fast Ethernet 1000BASE-T Gigabit Ethernet 1000BASE-T Gigabit Ethernet 100BASE-TX Fast Ethernet 100BASE-TX Fast Ethernet 10BASE-T Ethernet 10BASE-T Ethernet 155/622 Mbps ATM 155/622 Mbps ATM 4/16 Mbps Token Ring 4/16 Mbps Token Ring 100VG-AnyLAN 100VG-AnyLAN 100Mbps TP-PMD 100Mbps TP-PMD FAQ T-568B Wiring: There are two standards for wiring color code, 568A and 568B. While there's no difference in connectivity between 568A and 568B, 568B is the most prevalent wiring color code in the US. Our patch cable is 568B wired. T-568B Wiring: There are two standards for wiring color code, 568A and 568B. While there's no difference in connectivity between 568A and 568B, 568B is the most prevalent wiring color code in the US. Our patch cable is 568B wired. UTP and FTP: UTP is Unshielded Twisted Pair and FTP is Shielded Twisted Pair. FTP cable is wrapped in metal foil. Both have the same Ethernet communication performance, but FTP has better protection against Electro-Magnetis noise from outside. UTP and FTP: UTP is Unshielded Twisted Pair and FTP is Shielded Twisted Pair. FTP cable is wrapped in metal foil. Both have the same Ethernet communication performance, but FTP has better protection against Electro-Magnetis noise from outside. 24AWG and Stranded: AWG (American Wire Gauge) indicates wire thickness. Higher the number, thinner the wire. 24AWG or 26AWG is commonly used for ethernet cables. Stranded wire is a bundle of thin wires as oposed to solid wire that is single solid wire. 24AWG and Stranded: AWG (American Wire Gauge) indicates wire thickness. Higher the number, thinner the wire. 24AWG or 26AWG is commonly used for ethernet cables. Stranded wire is a bundle of thin wires as oposed to solid wire that is single solid wire.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51fM2apbHhL._SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"SF Cable","source_asin":"B0834RNSPD","category_path":"Electronics"},"sku":"BM-1191060","productType":"Electronics","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0834RNSPD","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"electronics-range.jsonl","source_asin":"B0834RNSPD","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
